ement from any device to all applications to minimize modern security risks and improve business efficiency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager for Okta Device Access, you will own key product areas and contribute to the continued evolution of ODA to meet customer and business needs. You will work closely with senior product leaders, engineering, and design to define how enterprise organizations secure and manage identity on Windows and macOS endpoints - from deploying the first device, to day two troubleshooting, to fleet level visibility. If you’re passionate about improving customer security and engaging with a vibrant community, we’re looking for you. Your primary responsibilities in these areas will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute the roadmap for the Okta Device Access Experience &amp;amp; Lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the administrator experience for fleets of devices with Okta Device Access across multiple platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the Okta-joined administrator experience end-to-end: from enrollment and provisioning to support troubleshooting to device lifecycle management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, design and research teams to define and document user stories and use-cases to guide product development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct research and analysis to identify customer needs and pain points, and use this information to inform innovation, product decisions and prioritization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with customers to deeply understand their challenges with respect to broad enterprise and consumer use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and communicate product requirements, including features, user experience, and technical specifications, to engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage product data to continually get smarter about how to improve our existing products, and work across the business to drive adoption and success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product Marketing to clearly articulate Okta&#39;s differentiation versus market alternatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Minimum Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across the product management lifecycle for enterprise products or services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills (presentation, verbal and written)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of successful delivery of complex projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of industry experience. 2+ years of product management or related experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred Skills:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Okta and how the technology works for Okta Device Access and Okta Verify&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with MDM Administrator experiences and device lifecycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with different MDMs such as Intune, Omnissa, etc are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with the competitive landscape in the device access management space&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
