&lt;p&gt;This is a key leadership role in the Professional Services (Technical Architecture) organization, responsible for the implementation of Okta services. The Senior Manager is an experienced, enthusiastic, and hands-on leader preferably in the Security and/or Identity &amp;amp; Access Management domain, who can rapidly learn and apply the Auth0 value proposition to customers of all sizes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Manager is a leader of a high-performing team of Technical Architects, functioning in a &quot;player-coach&quot; model. This role requires impressive field and management experience and involves mentoring the team of Technical Architects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have experience managing a technical team, resource forecasting, change &amp;amp; escalation management and operational excellence for Professional Service teams. You have a deep understanding of reporting and metrics as well as capacity planning and utilization targets. You will have a strong Consulting background with an ability to handle multiple work streams and be deeply comfortable with client issues and resolutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring, growing, and retaining a team of Professional Service Technical Architects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing direct management, mentoring, and support to ensure their continued technical, professional, and career growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Up-skilling team members to ensure they have the expertise to successfully deliver Okta to customers. Manages outlined objective and subjective performance metric requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active sync with Partner, delivery enablement &amp;amp; address performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acting as the primary customer liaison, managing relationships and communication between the project team, the customer, and internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring customer success from the beginning to the end of the engagement life cycle. Managing project budgets to meet customer and Okta expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Excellence:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting the Director with oversight and accountability for professional services billings, revenue, customer satisfaction, resources, and utilization. Demonstrating and improving a repeatable implementation methodology to rapidly enable customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform Governance &amp;amp; audits of Technical Architecture design and deliverables quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive team contribution to Technical Architecture Practice evolution and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly contribute to ongoing process improvement within the Technical Architecture practice and across Okta Professional Services and our subcontractor ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversight &amp;amp; manage of customer project dynamics, change management, concerns across multiple engagements and workstreams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years experience in Identity &amp;amp; Access Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience leading teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Design, consulting, delivering solutions to external customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in technologies and protocols like SAML 2.0, WS-Federation, OAuth, and OpenID Connect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of enterprise web technologies and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and multi-functionally supporting the development of client work you&#39;re doing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to Multi-task and manage multiple customer engagements is a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Process Improvement, Decision-making, Managing Processes, Planning, Analyzing Information and Developing Standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 50%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related discipline is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Auth0 Certified OR Okta Certified Consultant will be a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CISSP certification is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
