&lt;p&gt;The Senior Product Manager for the UI Platform is a high-impact individual contributor role, serving as a cornerstone for Okta&#39;s global user experience infrastructure. Joining the Product Platform group, you will own the foundational architecture that ensures every Okta product is elegant, scalable, and performant.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your role extends across owning the UI framework, design systems, localization/globalization frameworks, and accessibility (WCAG) standards, you provide the critical infrastructure that enables a cohesive, high-quality experience for Okta Workforce Identity products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Product Vision&lt;/strong&gt;: Define and champion the technical evolution of the Okta UI framework. Ensure the platform serves as a single source of truth for core administrative experiences across Okta products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Roadmap Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;: Prioritize and execute a complex roadmap across design systems, globalization, and accessibility. You will balance the needs of multiple product lines to ensure a unified developer and end-user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;: Partner with global engineering, design, and research teams to deliver infrastructure that supports Okta’s massive scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ecosystem Synthesis&lt;/strong&gt;: Engage with global customers and internal stakeholders to synthesize complex requirements into broad-value features that support a diverse, international ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: Leverage product data to optimize the developer experience for internal teams using the UI platform, defining and analyzing metrics that measure the performance and adoption of platform initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;North America Based Execution&lt;/strong&gt;: Lead the execution of the roadmap in direct partnership with development scrum teams (Engineering, UX, and Product) to deliver high-quality, resilient features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5-8+ years of Product Management experience&lt;/strong&gt; specifically within &lt;strong&gt;enterprise-scale SaaS platforms&lt;/strong&gt; or core software infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BS in Computer Science, Computer Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, or equivalent technical experience that enables you to rationalize and influence complex architectural decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven ability to produce solid, actionable plans&lt;/strong&gt; from incomplete, conflicting, or highly ambiguous inputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional communication and presentation skills&lt;/strong&gt;, with a track record of successfully collaborating across global functions and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated business results from platform capabilities or products you have shipped at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience managing design systems, UI frameworks, or core software platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with Identity and Access Management (IAM), digital security protocols, and enterprise infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in managing localization/globalization at scale and ensuring compliance with WCAG accessibility standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of user-centered design principles and agile development methodologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced degree in a technical field or an MBA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-MM&lt;br&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
