&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, assess, monitor, and report on operational, security, and compliance risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical automation across the risk management lifecycle by engineering custom AI agents, capabilities, and workflows to optimize risk data processing and scale operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate security control effectiveness, track deficiencies, and drive engineering remediation activities to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct root cause analysis on control deficiencies and post-incident reviews to identify underlying gaps and prevent recurrence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the risk owners to develop mitigation plans in line with the risk management strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern the formal risk acceptance and exception process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the risk register and issue lifecycle to deliver dynamic risk visibility to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply industry best practice for risk management across Okta, and provide insight into applying regulatory and industry frameworks to Okta’s security posture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong partnerships with cross functional teams to foster a cohesive view of security, compliance, and operational risks and drive remediation to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a security and technology subject matter expert within the security organization; provide critical advisory in the design and adoption of security controls, particularly those intended to meet regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop data analytics workflows and establish KRIs and KPIs to elevate team metrics and executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and continuously refine standardized risk assessment methodologies, playbooks, and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive security risk management program maturity and execution, aligning risk governance with the company’s goals and security strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive risk-awareness initiatives and champion a security-minded risk culture across business units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support ad hoc projects including program enhancements, security initiatives, and other GRC functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Requirements:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant BA/BS degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of hands-on security risk management and technical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building automated workflows, scripts (Python/APIs), and AI agentic solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry certification in security (CRISC, CISA, CISM, CISSP) or equivalent certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across regulations and common industry frameworks including but not limited to ISO, PCI, NIST CSF, COSO, and others.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred experience in Third-Party Risk Management, including hands-on execution of vendor security assessments and overall program operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of effectively influencing technical and business stakeholders to drive risk remediation and process adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of agile tools and GRC solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal, written, and interpersonal skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priority initiatives and deliver results under tight timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and adaptable to fast changing environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
