&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an execution-focused, highly technical &lt;strong&gt;Technical Account Manager (TAM)&lt;/strong&gt; specializing in enterprise identity, including Okta’s Workforce Identity Cloud (WIC) and Customer Identity Solutions (CIS).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will serve as a trusted technical advisor to mid-market and enterprise customer portfolios. You will cut through complexity, proactively optimize configurations, and guide customers on architectural best practices across hybrid SaaS, on-premise, and custom application environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a TAM at Okta, you embody a bias for action: you dig into technical details, eliminate architectural friction, and turn post-sales guidance into measurable customer traction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Proactive Technical Leadership &amp;amp; Customer Value&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Technical Guidance:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner as the technical counterpart to Customer Success Managers (CSMs) across mid-market and enterprise account portfolios, translating complex customer requirements into tangible business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Security Health Checks:&lt;/strong&gt; Audit customer Okta configurations and deployment architectures to continuously strengthen security posture, accelerate feature adoption, and drive ROI as Okta releases new features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retention &amp;amp; Health Acceleration:&lt;/strong&gt; Track and influence key account health metrics, using technical insight to drive product usage, reduce friction, and prevent churn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. High-Velocity Problem Solving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Escalation &amp;amp; Technical Advisory:&lt;/strong&gt; Address reactive technical inquiries and complex architectural blockers rapidly, breaking down multi-layered IAM challenges into simple, actionable steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive &amp;amp; Stakeholder Alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Build trusted technical relationships with C-level executives, IT directors, architects, and developers, establishing credibility as Okta’s subject matter expert.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Friction Elimination:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify recurring implementation bottlenecks across your account portfolio and partner with Product and Engineering to streamline workflows for customer teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Continuous Learning &amp;amp; Knowledge Enablement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product &amp;amp; Domain Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain deep, cutting-edge mastery across Workforce Identity Cloud (WIC), Customer Identity Solutions (CIS), and surrounding identity/security ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enablement &amp;amp; Content Creation:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive the creation of technical best-practice guides, architecture patterns, and enablement content for both internal TA teams and external customer groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Thrive in Technology Shifts:&lt;/strong&gt; Continuously adapt to emerging identity trends, security threats, and AI-driven identity capabilities, ensuring customer environments remain modern and resilient.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of total experience in information technology, with at least 3 years of hands-on experience as a Technical Account Manager (TAM) or comparable practitioner role in the IAM space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work US Time Zone (preference)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with IAM solution providers is strongly desired.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in any of the following: Technical Account Management, Technical Consulting, Solution Architect, Solutions Engineering, Product Management or similar role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of common software development practice. Understanding of identity and surrounding technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen, history of success owning enterprise segment customer relationships and escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills. Ability to set expectations and communicate goals and objectives with customers at various levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to track and influence customer behavior and health metrics across a portfolio of accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
